     Again, it's from Dungeons and Dragons.  The strength is represented 
as eighteen slash two-numbers (that's how it's read).  You're right, 
18.XX would be a little different, because for every /10 after the 
eighteen it's like having one more point of strength (i.e., 18/10 is 
really 19, 18/20 is 20, etc.).  (At least, that's how the modifiers in 
the AD&D Player's Handbook make it look.)  That means your strength can be 
far more developed than any other attribute (useful for describing giants' 
strength).
